From efe09b50033becfdb2d38f7737fd9471897b9bf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 07:25:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(migrate): fold external_ref/started_at + read split
 .beads layout

Fable-review honesty fix: issues.external_ref (6 issues, e.g. gh-88) and
issues.started_at were silently dropped with NO gap entry, contradicting the
"sole remaining gap" claim. Both now fold into the issue metadata blob
(metadata.beads_external_ref / metadata.beads_started_at), matching the
owner -> metadata.beads_owner handling. Documented that beads-internal/derived
fields (content_hash, etc.) are intentionally not carried; the only remaining
reported gap is now genuinely dependencies.created_by.

Also make loadBeadsSnapshotFromDirectory tolerant of the SPLIT .beads layout
(events under .beads/backup/, interactions at .beads/interactions.jsonl): a
file missing from the given dir is also read from a backup/ subdir and the
parent dir, so pointing --source at either location no longer silently
half-reads the memory/activity sidecars. Fixed the owner-trim comparison so a
padded assignee/created_by no longer double-stores the owner.

Tests: external_ref/started_at survive into metadata; owner not double-stored;
split-layout loading. CHANGELOG wording corrected. Regenerated the D20 artifact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
